                <pb facs="0386" n="371" xml:id="pg371"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On January 12 Bevin and Cripps told Harriman that they agreed that OEEC operations should be strengthened at the
                    ministerial level. Bevin supported a proposal by Cripps for executive direction
                    by five ministers (Spaak as chairman, and vice chairmen from the United Kingdom,
                    France, Italy, and one of the Scandinavian countries), with preliminary steps to
                    be taken in London looking toward a ministerial meeting in mid-February.
                    Harriman concluded that the British favored a stronger political structure for
                    the OEEC but still had reservations concerning
                    the operating organization. (Telegram Repto
                    2285 from Paris, January 14, not printed, ECA
                    Telegram Files, FRC Acc. No. 53A278, Paris Repto)</p>
                <p>For additional information on the structure and activities of the OEEC, see its various publications and reports,
                    including <hi rendition="#italic">The Organisation for European Economic
                        Co-operation: Two Years of Economic Co-operation</hi> (Paris, 1950).</p>
            </div>
